            <ArticleTitle>An audit of pain/discomfort experienced during image-guided breast biopsy procedures.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>398-402</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A prospective audit of 221 breast biopsies was carried out to assess the pain/discomfort experienced during image-guided breast biopsies. The only significant factor in pain scores was the size of the needle used. Fine-needle aspiration cytology using a 21-gauge needle was found to cause the most discomfort.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
